=== an aggregate in WHERE names the clause that does accept it
--- SELECT count() AS c FROM numbers(10) WHERE c > 1
Code: 184. Aggregate function count() AS c is found in WHERE in query. Aggregate functions are not allowed in WHERE and PREWHERE, because they are computed after filtering; use HAVING to filter by the result of an aggregation. (ILLEGAL_AGGREGATION)
--- SELECT count() FROM numbers(10) WHERE count() > 1
Code: 184. Aggregate function count() is found in WHERE in query. Aggregate functions are not allowed in WHERE and PREWHERE, because they are computed after filtering; use HAVING to filter by the result of an aggregation. (ILLEGAL_AGGREGATION)
--- SELECT count() FROM t PREWHERE count() > 1
Code: 184. Aggregate function count() is found in PREWHERE in query. Aggregate functions are not allowed in WHERE and PREWHERE, because they are computed after filtering; use HAVING to filter by the result of an aggregation. (ILLEGAL_AGGREGATION)
--- SELECT count() AS c FROM numbers(10) WHERE c > 1 SETTINGS enable_analyzer = 0
Code: 184. Aggregate function count() is found in WHERE in query. Aggregate functions are not allowed in WHERE and PREWHERE, because they are computed after filtering; use HAVING to filter by the result of an aggregation: While processing count() AS c. (ILLEGAL_AGGREGATION)
10

=== a value that is not a date is not reported as being too short
--- SELECT toDate('yesterday')
Code: 38. Cannot parse date: expected a date in the YYYY-MM-DD or YYYYMMDD format: Cannot parse Date from String
--- SELECT toDate('202')
Code: 38. Cannot parse date: expected a date in the YYYY-MM-DD or YYYYMMDD format: Cannot parse Date from String
--- SELECT toDate('abcd-01-02')
Code: 38. Cannot parse date here: abcd-01-02: Cannot parse Date from String
2020-01-02
